      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2025-02-14T20:07:51Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-14T20:07:51Z",
    "body": "> Feel free to give me a shout if you want to explain what you think I'm missing and I can probably work out the missing piece myself.\r\n\r\nAlright, I think I'm happy with the latest [Chromium CL behavior](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6259116). I've added more corner cases to the `the-dialog-element/dialog-closedby.html` test that hopefully exercises many more weird situations. E.g. calling `showModal()` or `close()` from the `focusin` handler that gets called when focus is restored while running `close()`, or from the `beforetoggle` event, etc.\r\n\r\nI think this is the end state that seems to make the most sense:\r\n- Define \"do cleanup\" to be the removal of `dialog` from the document's \"open dialogs list\", **and** destroying/nullifying the `dialog`'s close watcher.\r\n- Define \"do setup\" to be the opposite of that (add to the dialog list and create the close watcher).\r\n- When the `dialog`'s `open` attribute is removed **while the dialog is connected**, \"do cleanup\".\r\n- When a `dialog` with the `open` attribute is removed from the document (**and** a state preserving atomic move is **not** in progress), \"do cleanup\".\r\n- When the `dialog`'s `open` attribute is added **while the dialog is connected**, \"do setup\".\r\n- When a `dialog` with the `open` attribute is inserted into the document (**and** a state preserving atomic move is **not** in progress), \"do setup\".\r\n- Make sure to \"do cleanup\" prior to performing the \"focus the previously focused element\" algorithm in `.close()`.\r\n\r\nNote that if we do the above, and before landing some version of https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10124, there will still be [this list of behaviors that are still \"different\" when removing the `open` attribute as compared to calling `.close()`](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10953#issuecomment-2643608252).\r\n",
