    "updated_at": "2025-03-07T15:50:09Z",
    "body": "I just looked into this and I think we don't actually need any changes here. This is because of a difference in spec layout vs chromium impl. In chrome the RemovedFrom and InsertedInto methods are invoked and the then there's early returns for state preserving atomic move operations. However, the spec went a different approach and defined separate moving steps.\r\n\r\nBecause we don't have moving steps defined for dialog, nothing happens to it which is expected.\r\n\r\n@mfreed7 @domfarolino does this make sense to you or am I missing something?",
