    "updated_at": "2025-06-06T21:38:03Z",
    "body": "> But fingers crossed that nothing needs to change here.\r\n\r\nYeah, @lukewarlow is right in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10954#issuecomment-2706794751, this PR does not have to consider the state-preserving atomic move case from the insertion/removal steps, since those are not triggered during moves.\r\n\r\n----\r\n\r\nUnrelated, what is the status of this PR? It seems to be getting close to landed and has lots of work and discussion poured into it, but it's still in a \"draft\" state it seems?",
